<h1>About HackShack Labs</h1>
<p>HackShack Labs is an independent technology publication by <strong>Ploos AS</strong>. We cover open technology, self-hosting, privacy, networking, retro computing and practical hardware projects. English is our original editorial language; Norwegian Bokmål is an additional translation.</p>
<h2>How we label evidence</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Documentation-based:</strong> based on technical documentation, not a physical test.</li><li><strong>Desk research:</strong> analysis of documented sources, listings or specifications without direct hardware verification.</li><li><strong>Lab-tested:</strong> a described experiment was performed with recorded methods and limitations.</li><li><strong>Hardware verified:</strong> the stated procedure or claim was checked on identified physical hardware and firmware.</li></ul>
<p>A status label applies only to the evidence actually described. No article is hardware verified simply because it contains technical instructions. We correct errors and update articles when evidence changes; substantial corrections should be noted with a date.</p>
<h2>Commercial independence</h2>
<p>Affiliate relationships may fund this publication. Qualifying links are marked, and recommendations are not purchased. We consider alternatives regardless of whether we earn a commission. Sponsorships and review samples must be disclosed where applicable.</p>
<h2>Support independent research</h2>
<p>HackShack Labs articles remain free to read. Voluntary contributions help fund test hardware, lab upkeep and practical guides; they do not buy editorial influence or guarantee a particular review. <a href="https://ko-fi.com/hackshacklabs" rel="noopener noreferrer">Support HackShack Labs on Ko-fi</a>.</p>
<h2>Licensing and reuse</h2>
<p>Unless an article states otherwise, original editorial text is offered under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0)</a>. Third-party images, trademarks and linked resources retain their respective rights. Check any article-specific notices.</p>
<h2>Corrections and contact</h2>
<p>To suggest a correction or report an issue, use the <a href="https://github.com/Ploos-AS/hackshack-labs/issues">public issue tracker</a>. Please include the article URL and evidence, and do not post private information.</p>
